From a3ad3f421de15b98b5ba171aafd1a3586c4a5b56 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: haowen1993 <39072333+haowen1993@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 00:47:48 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 05/10] fix(art): show Chinese art when the card's default
 printing lacks it
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Reported: Temple of Mystery and Time Wipe showed English art although a Chinese
version of each exists. Both were real findings, and neither was a missing
translation:

  Temple of Mystery  default soc #414 (2026)  → no Chinese; who #318 has it
  Time Wipe          default tdc #308 (2025)  → no Chinese; who #238 has it

The app renders the printing named in `scryfall-data.json`, which is the newest
one. Within one card's printings the Chinese split is arbitrary and not derivable
from any Scryfall field: the CDN localizes community art under the ENGLISH
printing's id, and inside Doctor Who #318 of a card has it while #528, #909 and
#1119 do not. Measured across all 1178 Doctor Who printings: 398 (33%).

So availability is measured once (`scryfall-images.zhs-available.json`, 15 KB,
probed with GET + Range: bytes=0-0) and consulted at resolution time. When the
printing the stored asset names has no art in the active derived locale, the
first printing that does is used instead. Costs the printings map on that path,
which is why it is gated on a derived locale AND a miss.

Verified end to end: both cards now resolve to their WHO printing and serve
200 image/webp; the art was inspected and is the Chinese card.
